diff --git a/crates/rightkit-llm/CHANGELOG.md b/crates/rightkit-llm/CHANGELOG.md
index 48a0e56..08c3f78 100644
--- a/crates/rightkit-llm/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/crates/rightkit-llm/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,32 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.4.0 (unreleased)
+
+Breaking (minor bump for 0.x):
+
+- **Breaking:** `LlmError::Status` gains `retry_after: Option<Duration>` (the provider's `Retry-After`, parsed). Code that builds `Status` by struct literal needs the field; a pattern that names every field needs `..`. New `LlmError::retry_after()` looks through the capture and billing wrappers.
+- **Breaking:** `LlmError` gains the variant `IncompleteOutput { cause, partial }` (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#657), so exhaustive matches need an arm. It is returned only when a `StreamPolicy` is set.
+- **Breaking:** `generation::ImageRequest` gains `count` and `output_format`; `ImageRoute` gains `output_formats`, `provider` and `base_url` and its `sizes` are `Vec<ImageSize>` (a size is still the string `1024x1024` in JSON). Code that builds these by struct literal needs the new fields (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#663).
+
+Added:
+
+- Stream policy (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#657): module `stream` (`StreamPolicy { idle, semantic_progress, require_finish }`, `IncompleteCause`, `PartialOutput`, `PartialToolCall`). `with_stream_policy` on `OpenAiCompatProvider`, `AnthropicProvider`, `OpenAiResponsesProvider` and the async providers. `require_finish` turns EOF without `[DONE]`, a finish reason, `message_stop` or `response.completed` (or inside an unterminated frame) into `LlmError::IncompleteOutput`, never a short answer. `semantic_progress` fails when no text, tool-call or reasoning delta arrived for the limit although keep-alive frames kept coming (Anthropic `ping`, empty OpenAI chunks); `idle` fails when no frame arrived. `partial` carries text, reasoning, tool calls and usage; `LlmError::billing()` reports its usage; a partial with output is not a failover trigger. The blocking providers check the clock when a frame arrives (a silent connection needs `ClientConfig::idle_timeout`, reported as `Idle`); the async providers use a timer. Streams now also collect `reasoning_content` and Anthropic thinking text into `partial.reasoning`.
+- Per-physical-attempt observation (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#658): module `attempts`. `ObservedProvider` wraps any `Provider`, makes each attempt with the inner retries off, and reports `AttemptEvent::Attempt` (with a `SubmissionReceipt`: `Submitted`, `Rejected`, `SubmissionUnknown`) and `AttemptEvent::RetryScheduled` ("retrying in N s (reason)"). `AttemptLadder` keeps two budgets apart: connection failures climb a list of waits, HTTP status failures get exponential backoff that honours `Retry-After` up to a cap. An unknown outcome is not replayed unless `retry_unknown` is set. `receipt_for` and `is_connect_failure` are public. A stream is retried only before its first event. With feature `async`, `AsyncObservedProvider` does the same for an `AsyncProvider` (waits on the tokio timer; a stream is retried while it is being opened).
+- OpenAI Responses API (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#665): module `responses`, `OpenAiResponsesProvider`, `ResponsesVariant::{OpenAi, ChatGptCodex}`, `build_body`, `parse_response`. Messages map to input items (`function_call`, `function_call_output`), `system` to `instructions`, a response schema to `text.format`. The ChatGPT-OAuth variant posts to `/codex/responses`, always streams, sends `store: false` and leaves out `max_output_tokens` and `temperature`. Its field details are unverified against the live endpoint (module docs).
+- Model capability catalogue (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#662): module `capability`. `CapabilityCatalogue` rows carry tier, reasoning depth 0-3, supported efforts, tool-schema class, vision, context window and a `Compaction` rule (trigger percent, reserve tokens, max summary output tokens); `AliasRule` maps provider-native names; lookup is exact, never prefix. `CapabilityStore` keeps a signed `snapshot.json` and `last-known-good.json`: `install` verifies through a host `SnapshotVerifier` (digest and signature), refuses an older version and changes nothing on failure; `load` falls back to the last-known-good snapshot and reports `degraded`.
+- Subscription auth (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#583): module `auth`. `RequestAuth` supplies per-request headers (`RequestHeader::{Bearer, Secret, Plain}`); `with_request_auth` on the OpenAI-compatible, Anthropic and Responses providers replaces the `CredentialSource` for that provider. `CredentialAuth` builds them from a `CredentialSource`. Feature `oauth` adds `SubscriptionAuth` over `rightkit_oauth::credentials::Resolver` (refreshing stored sign-in, `Eligibility` check, `sign_in_device`, `save` for loopback PKCE results) and `CredentialStore` (= `rightkit_oauth::TokenStore`).
+- Provider record and replay (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#585): module `replay`. `RecordingProvider` and `Recorder` append calls to a JSON Lines corpus (opt-in: `Recorder::from_env`), `Redactor` blanks credential keys and registered secrets, every line carries a schema version and `recorded_at`, `ReplayProvider` answers from a `Corpus` and refuses entries older than 90 days. It works at the `Provider` seam; `rightkit-http` has no pluggable transport, so the HTTP request builder is not exercised by a replay.
+- Async providers (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#656), feature `async`: module `async_provider`. `AsyncProvider`, `AsyncOpenAiCompatProvider`, `AsyncAnthropicProvider`, `AsyncOpenAiResponsesProvider` on `rightkit_http::AsyncClient`; `complete` and `stream` (an `EventStream`, a `futures_util::Stream` of `StreamEvent` with the assembled response at the end; dropping it aborts the request). `complete_wire` / `stream_wire` send caller-owned wire JSON verbatim so a host keeps lossless reasoning, thinking and tool-result history. `PreSend` runs on the exact bytes before send for a capacity gate or authority check. `AsyncImageGenerationClient`.
+- Anthropic cache control plan (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#656): `cache::CacheControlPlan` and `CacheAnchor` (last tool, first or last system block, trailing message) with `AnthropicProvider::with_cache_plan`, `AsyncAnthropicProvider::with_cache_plan` and `anthropic::build_body_with_plan`.
+- Async failover (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#661), feature `async`: module `async_failover`, `AsyncFailoverChain` and `AsyncRoute` with the blocking chain's rules (retryable-only by default, first-token timeout, circuit breaker, `FailoverEvent` with `breaker_skipped`). A caller `Classifier` sees each error before `FailoverOn`; `FailoverChain::classify` adds the same hook to the blocking chain.
+- Image generation (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#663): `ImageGenerationClient::generate_all` returns every image (`count` 1 to 4), `ImageRequest::with_count` and `with_output_format` (`OutputFormat`), typed `ImageSize`, `ImageRoute::check`, `ImageRouteCatalogue::provider_for_base_url` (exact catalogued endpoint only), `parse_images`. `from_json` is the supported loader; a TOML loader would add a parser dependency.
+- Tool-call reassembly (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#664): `ToolCallChunkReassembler::drain_completed_lenient` (never fails, index order, empty id or name stays empty), `ToolCallChunkReassembler::first_wins` (a repeated id or name that differs is ignored), `is_empty`.
+- Resumable skill executor (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#296): module `skill`. `SkillRunner` runs a `SkillPlan` of `Step`s (`FnStep`, `ModelStep` with `gate` and a repair ceiling, `BatchStep` with one checkpoint per item) and saves `RunState` to a `CheckpointStore` (`MemoryCheckpointStore`, `FileCheckpointStore`) before dispatch, after completion and after each `StepResult::Continue`. Resume after a crash does not replay a `Paid` or `Commit` step whose outcome is unknown (`RunStatus::Unresolved`, settled with `Resolution`); a `Commit` step runs at most once; a changed `base` is `SkillError::StaleBase`; a `Budget` (calls, input and output tokens, USD, `require_price`) stops the run before the call; a cancel flag interrupts at the next boundary.
+- Token counting (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#417): module `tokens`. `TokenCounter` (the seam for an exact tokenizer), `EstimateCounter` (dependency-free: one token per four ASCII bytes plus one per non-ASCII character, always flagged inexact), `count_request` (system, messages, tool-use and tool-result blocks, tool definitions, images at a fixed estimate, framing `Overhead`), `fits` and `trim_to_budget`. An exact `o200k` counter is not included: it needs a vocabulary file or a tokenizer dependency.
+- New features: `async` (`rightkit-http/async`, `futures-util`, `tokio` timers) and `oauth` (`rightkit-oauth` with `secrets`).
+
+Not in this release: the canonical-JSON and ignore-aware repository walk parts of Orthic-Labs/rightkit#417 belong to `rightkit-contracts` and `rightkit-fsindex`; lossless `ContentBlock` variants for signed thinking blocks (the wire-history input carries them instead); raw response capture on the async providers.
+
 ## 0.3.0 (2026-10-17)
 
 - **Breaking:** public route-health registry retains at most 256 routes & 32 KiB of route-name bytes. Outcome records & state reads refresh LRU order; new routes evict oldest observations. Evicted routes read as `Healthy` until reporting again; oversized names are ignored. `snapshot` lists currently retained routes. Owned `RouteHealth` state & independent `FailoverChain` breakers are unchanged.
