+//! Async providers on `rightkit_http::AsyncClient` (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#656, #665, #663).
+//! Feature `async`; a tokio runtime is needed at call time.
+//!
+//! [`AsyncProvider`] is the async counterpart of [`crate::provider::Provider`]:
+//!
+//! - `complete(req)` returns the whole [`ChatResponse`].
+//! - `stream(req)` resolves when the response headers arrive (a 4xx or 5xx is an `Err` here,
+//!   before any token, so a failover chain can move on) and yields an [`EventStream`]: a
+//!   `futures_util::Stream` of `Result<StreamEvent, LlmError>`. When it ends, or after the
+//!   first `Err`, [`EventStream::response`] holds the assembled [`ChatResponse`]; or call
+//!   [`EventStream::finish`] to drain and get it.
+//! - **Drop to cancel.** Dropping the [`EventStream`] drops the HTTP body, which aborts the
+//!   request and closes the connection. Dropping the `stream()` future before it resolves does
+//!   the same.
+//!
+//! Three providers share the trait: [`AsyncOpenAiCompatProvider`] (chat completions),
+//! [`AsyncAnthropicProvider`] (Messages, with an optional [`CacheControlPlan`]) and
+//! [`AsyncOpenAiResponsesProvider`] (Responses and the ChatGPT-OAuth `/codex/responses`).
+//!
+//! # Input
+//!
+//! Each takes either a [`ChatRequest`] (`complete`, `stream`) or pre-built wire JSON
+//! (`complete_wire`, `stream_wire`): the caller's OpenAI-shaped or Anthropic-shaped request
+//! body, sent verbatim except that the stream flags are set by `stream_wire`. Wire input is how
+//! a host keeps a lossless history (reasoning content, signed thinking blocks, tool results with
+//! error flags): it stores the provider's own JSON and replays it.
+//!
+//! # Pre-send hook
+//!
+//! [`PreSend`] runs between request preparation and send with the exact bytes about to be
+//! sent ([`PreparedRequest::body`]). A host runs its capacity gate and request-authority check
+//! there; returning `Err` stops the call before anything is sent.
+//!
+//! # Not included
+//!
+//! Raw response capture ([`crate::raw`]) and the `Captured` error wrapper exist only on the
+//! blocking providers.
+
+use std::collections::VecDeque;
+use std::future::Future;
+use std::pin::Pin;
+use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};
+use std::task::{Context, Poll};
+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};
+
+use futures_util::{Stream, StreamExt};
+use rightkit_http::{AsyncClient, EofPolicy, HttpError, Request, SseEvent, SseStream};
+use serde_json::{json, Value};
+
+use crate::anthropic::{self, Assembler};
+use crate::auth::{RequestAuth, ResolveRequest};
+use crate::cache::CacheControlPlan;
+use crate::credentials::CredentialSource;
+use crate::error::LlmError;
+use crate::generation::{self, GeneratedImage, ImageRequest};
+use crate::openai::{self, MaxTokensField, OpenAiStream};
+use crate::responses::{self, ResponsesStream, ResponsesVariant};
+use crate::stream::{IncompleteCause, ProgressClock, StreamPolicy};
+use crate::types::*;
